            <ArticleTitle>Menstrual bleeding from an endometriotic lesion.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1926-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.fertnstert.2008.08.125</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case in which endometriotic lesions were observed to be focally hemorrhagic at laparoscopy performed during menstruation. Red vesicular lesions likely represent early disease with intact capacity for hormonally induced menstrual bleeding.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
